  "worked_solution": "The expression has three terms: $7x,$ $-\\frac{2}{9}y,$ and $-3z.$ Each of these terms contains a variable, so none of them are constant terms.\n\nThe constant term is missing. However, we can include it by adding zero to the expression. Rewriting the given expression as\n\n$$\n7x-\\frac{2}{9}y-3z+0,\n$$\n\nwe see that the value of the constant term is $0.$",
